Subject: Supply Chain Due Diligence Request — Alleged Labor Rights Violations at Your Supplier {{company}}

Dear Compliance & Sustainability Team,

I am a (former) employee of {{company}} ("the Supplier"), which I understand is part of your supply chain. I am writing to formally request that you investigate the alleged labor-law violations described below, in accordance with the EU Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive (CSDDD, Directive (EU) 2024/1760) and your Supplier Code of Conduct.

1. Supplier details
Company name: {{company}}
Registration No.: {{creditCode}}
Registered address: {{address}}

2. Allegations
- {{violation}};
- {{detail}};
- {{evidence}}.

3. Actions requested
- Launch a due diligence review of the above allegations under the CSDDD and your supply chain compliance framework;
- Require the Supplier to take corrective action within a reasonable timeframe and report back on the outcome;
- If the allegations are confirmed, apply the appropriate remedies under your supplier management policy.

4. Supporting documents
- Employment contract and any dismissal / reassignment notices;
- Payroll statements and attendance records;
- Chat records, audio recordings and other evidence (available on request).

I confirm that the information set out above is accurate to the best of my knowledge, and I am available to cooperate fully with your investigation.

Yours faithfully,
{{name}}
Tel: {{phone}}   Email: {{email}}
Date: {{date}}
